ce of the vocabulary (createmeta? config block? per-project field?) is not stated.","Scope lists value_maps.py and the create path but no vocabulary-declaration surface."],"finding":"The 'declared priority vocabulary' referenced by the fail-closed validation has no stated source or declaration mechanism — how/where a project declares its priority vocabulary is unspecified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff8c72f36adfb6614","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach (final sentence)","norm_id":"n778a02364be71c71","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor must implement the fail-closed check but cannot tell where the vocabulary is declared or read from."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct or ground the Approach's 'declared priority vocabulary' validation claim: mapping_config.validate() does NOT vocabulary-check priority_map (capability-gated only per its own docstring), and no priority-vocabulary declaration exists in S1 — either drop the sentence or explicitly scope adding a priority vocabulary + its _check_vocab wiring.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.25,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["mapping_config.py validate() (lines 328-359): _check_vocab invoked for status_map/type_map/link_map only; priority_map gets only _check_capability","mapping_config.py validate() docstring lines 336-337: 'priority_map has no vocabulary list (capability-gated only)'","mapping_config.py MappingLayer vocab fields are statuses/issue_types/link_types/hierarchy — no priority vocabulary; search for 'priorities' in the module finds only the has_priorities capability bool","docs/config.md:550 shows [mapping.default.priority_map] with no partner priority-vocabulary declaration"],"finding":"The Approach asserts an S1 validation guarantee that does not exist: 'Validation (S1) fails closed if a priority_map value is outside the declared priority vocabulary when one is declared.' In mapping_config.py, priority_map is capability-gated ONLY (has_priorities) and is never vocabulary-validated — validate() calls _check_vocab for status_map/type_map/link_map but not priority_map, and the docstring states plainly 'priority_map has no vocabulary list (capability-gated only)'. There is no priority-vocabulary declaration field (only statuses/issue_types/link_types/hierarchy exist).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcf121b731b0d1af8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section — final sentence ('Validation (S1) fails closed if a priority_map value is outside the declared priority vocabulary when one is declared.')","norm_id":"n0c51ca656ea8e6bc","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer or implementer relies on the plan's claim that S1 already fails closed on out-of-vocabulary priority values, when no such vocabulary or check exists","The plan is treated as introducing NO new validation, but delivering the described guarantee would require adding a new priority-vocabulary axis to S1 — unscoped work"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Reword to match S1 as built: 'Validation (S1) already capability-gates priority_map (a non-empty priority_map with has_priorities=False fails closed); there is no priority vocabulary check.' If a vocabulary check is actually wanted, add it to Scope as new work on mapping_config.py (a priorities vocabulary field + _check_vocab call).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate the priority-mapping consumers a config-driven priority_map must thread through (outbound_mapper.map_fields_to_remote at line 144, DC _map_local_to_dc_fields at backend.py:87, acli.py:175, acli_cli_ops.py:359) and name the effective-priority-map resolver, rather than scoping only value_maps.py.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["search 'effective_priority_map' -> (no matches); no resolver analogous to config.effective_status_map exists","LOCAL_PRIORITY_TO_JIRA.get(...) is called directly at outbound_mapper.py:144 (UPDATE), adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:87 (CREATE), adapters/jira/acli.py:175, adapters/jira/acli_cli_ops.py:359","status_map is threaded through map_fields_to_remote / map_local_to_remote / _effective_status_map_for as the precedent; the plan's Scope lists none of these priority consumers"],"finding":"Making priority 'config-driven' by resolving an effective priority map requires threading that map into the priority-mapping consumers, but the plan's Scope names only value_maps.py and does not enumerate them; there is no effective_priority_map resolver and priority is mapped inline via LOCAL_PRIORITY_TO_JIRA.get(...) at multiple sites.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f21c22efb2516893c","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope + Approach ('priority built-in default becomes injected fallback' / 'resolve the effective priority map')","norm_id":"nc97dc8a4a9c85afc","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A priority_map override is configured but the UPDATE mapper (outbound_mapper.py:144) still reads the hardcoded built-in because no map is threaded in","DC create path (backend.py:87) ignores the override because it maps priority inline"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add an effective_priority_map resolver (mirroring config.effective_status_map) and list the create/update sites that must accept and apply it in Scope.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the priority-vocabulary validation claim with mapping_config.py:336-337 (priority_map has no vocabulary list, capability-gated only): either drop the vocabulary-based validation or explicitly scope creating a new priority vocabulary axis.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["mapping_config.py:336-337: 'priority_map has no vocabulary list (capability-gated only); create_defaults is ungated.'","validate() calls _check_vocab only for status_map/type_map/link_map (lines 357-359); priority_map gets only _check_capability against has_priorities","No 'priorities' vocabulary field exists on MappingLayer analogous to statuses/issue_types/link_types"],"finding":"The Approach/Acceptance says validation 'fails closed if a priority_map value is outside the declared priority vocabulary when one is declared', but no priority vocabulary axis exists — mapping_config.validate explicitly documents priority_map as having no vocabulary list (capability-gated only).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe673217fb00266bd","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach ('outside the declared priority vocabulary when one is declared')","norm_id":"nb511aae6cf09b35b","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer tries to validate priority_map against a declared vocabulary and finds no such axis to check against"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the specific create-payload assembly site(s) — Cloud outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields and DC _map_local_to_dc_fields — and the map_local_to_remote signature/caller (outbound_mutation_builders.py:87) that must plumb create_defaults through.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0556,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["map_local_to_remote is defined on both backends: adapters/jira/backend.py:73 (delegates to outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields) and adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:121 (delegates to _map_local_to_dc_fields)","Current map_local_to_remote signature has params binding_store/local_ticket_types/emit_detach_clear/suppressed_out/status_map — no create_defaults or mapping arg","outbound_mutation_builders.py:87 is the caller that would need to source create_defaults from mapping"],"finding":"Scope names 'the issue-create path in the reconciler outbound (create payload assembly)' as a single site, but there are two distinct create-payload bodies (Cloud outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields and DC _map_local_to_dc_fields), and map_local_to_remote's current signature carries no create_defaults/mapping parameter to merge into.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f26327ed2f5a78f39","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope (second bullet)","norm_id":"ne6db6a12429a0c04","priority":0.7556,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["create_defaults merged into only the Cloud body, silently absent on DC creates (or vice versa)"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the int-keyed built-in priority map and the string-keyed [mapping.priority_map] config are normalized to one key type before merge (so an overlay actually overrides), and assert the overlay overrides through the real merge in test_priority_config_effect.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["value_maps.py:22 `LOCAL_PRIORITY_TO_JIRA: dict[int, str]` uses integer keys 0-4","mapping_config._parse_axis_map returns `dict[str, str]` and docs/config.md:550-551 shows `[mapping.default.priority_map]` `2 = \"Medium\"` (TOML table keys are strings)","_merge_axis (mapping_config.py:238) does `merged.update(overlay)`: a string key '2' will NOT override the int key 2, so the overlay adds a dead entry and the int lookup still hits the built-in"],"finding":"The plan does not reconcile the key-type mismatch between the int-keyed built-in priority map and the string-keyed config axis, so a priority_map overlay would silently fail to override.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f35413c3e5f7c5b86","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — Priority; Scope (value_maps.py bullet)","norm_id":"na1cd8fd6a80fbe8c","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator sets [mapping.projects.REB.priority_map] 2 = \"P3\"; outbound priority still resolves to the built-in \"Medium\" because the lookup key is int 2, not str '2'"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Inject the built-in as a string-keyed layer (`{\"0\":\"Highest\",...}`) and look up priority by `str(value)` at the emission boundary, mirroring the string-keyed status seam; or convert the resolved map back to int keys after resolve_for_project. State the chosen normalization in the Approach.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend Scope to the UPDATE mapper (outbound_mapper.py) and DC create path, and introduce a `resolve_outbound_priority` + `effective_priority_map` seam mirroring the existing `resolve_outbound_status`/`config.effective_status_map`, so map-or-drift has ONE implementation across create and update on both deployments.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Scope names only `value_maps.py` and 'the issue-create path (create payload assembly)'","Unmapped priority is currently COERCED to \"Medium\" at three sites: outbound_mapper.py:144 (UPDATE mapper), adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:144 (Cloud create), adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:87 (DC create)","The status axis already has resolve_outbound_status (outbound_mapper.py:47) + config.effective_status_map (config.py:77) implementing exactly this omit-and-warn drift; no effective_priority_map / resolve_outbound_priority exists (search returned no matches)"],"finding":"The plan's priority drift semantics ('leave Jira's value, warn') require changing the actual mapping sites, but Scope omits the UPDATE mapper and the DC create path and does not introduce a priority resolver seam analogous to the existing status seam.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f55a30a0d6ba20bb5","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope — priority bullets; Approach — Priority","norm_id":"nb84d9f3730eba26e","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An unmapped priority on an UPDATE still coerces to \"Medium\" (outbound_mapper.py:144) because that path is out of scope","A DC create still coerces to \"Medium\" (backend.py:87) — priority drift is Cloud-create-only, contradicting 'a soft field ... leave Jira's value'"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add `resolve_outbound_priority(value, priority_map) -> str | None` next to resolve_outbound_status returning None (omit + deduped warn) on an unmapped priority, and route all three current .get(...,'Medium') sites through it via a config.effective_priority_map resolver.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion + test proving S1 validation rejects a priority_map value outside a declared priority vocabulary (fail-